Relevant columns and their potential usage  
`primary_type`: filter rows to the crime category “MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT”.  
`date`: extract year / month to build monthly counts.  
`year`: an already‑materialised year value that can be used for coarse filtering (optional – `date` works as well).  

Typical conditions  
• `primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'` – keeps only motor‑vehicle theft crimes.  
• `EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date)` BETWEEN 2010 AND 2016 – restricts the time window.  

Below are ten progressively richer BigQuery SQL queries (all different; each capped with `LIMIT 20`).  
Use them in order to explore the data and finally obtain the required result.

```sql
-- 1. Peek at a handful of rows to see the structure of motor‑vehicle theft records
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
WHERE primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. List all distinct primary crime categories that exist
SELECT DISTINCT primary_type
FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Show the distinct years present in the data set
SELECT DISTINCT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) AS yr
FROM `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
ORDER BY yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Count total motor‑vehicle thefts that happened in each year (any month)
SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date)   AS yr,
       COUNT(*)                  AS thefts_in_year
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
WHERE  primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'
GROUP  BY yr
ORDER  BY yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Get monthly counts (year & month) just for 2010 as a sanity check
SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR  FROM date) AS yr,
       EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date) AS mo,
       COUNT(*)                 AS thefts_in_month
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
WHERE  primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'
  AND  EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) = 2010
GROUP  BY yr, mo
ORDER  BY mo
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. The same monthly counts, but for *all* years 2010‑2016
SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR  FROM date) AS yr,
       EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date) AS mo,
       COUNT(*)                 AS thefts_in_month
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
WHERE  primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'
  AND  EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) BETWEEN 2010 AND 2016
GROUP  BY yr, mo
ORDER  BY yr, mo
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Add a window function to see each month’s count and its rank within the year
SELECT yr,
       mo,
       thefts_in_month,
       RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY yr ORDER BY thefts_in_month DESC) AS rnk_in_year
FROM (
    SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date)  AS yr,
           EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date) AS mo,
           COUNT(*)                AS thefts_in_month
    FROM   `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
    WHERE  primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'
      AND  EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) BETWEEN 2010 AND 2016
    GROUP  BY yr, mo
)
ORDER BY yr, rnk_in_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Keep only the top‑ranked (highest) month per year by using the window rank
SELECT yr,
       mo,
       thefts_in_month
FROM (
    SELECT yr,
           mo,
           thefts_in_month,
           RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY yr ORDER BY thefts_in_month DESC) AS rnk_in_year
    FROM (
        SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date)  AS yr,
               EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date) AS mo,
               COUNT(*)                AS thefts_in_month
        FROM   `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
        WHERE  primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'
          AND  EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) BETWEEN 2010 AND 2016
        GROUP  BY yr, mo
    )
)
WHERE rnk_in_year = 1
ORDER BY yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Same result as #8 but via a HAVING‑MAX approach (no window functions)
SELECT yr,
       MAX(thefts_in_month) AS highest_monthly_thefts
FROM (
    SELECT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date)  AS yr,
           EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date) AS mo,
           COUNT(*)                AS thefts_in_month
    FROM   `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
    WHERE  primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'
      AND  EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) BETWEEN 2010 AND 2016
    GROUP  BY yr, mo
)
GROUP BY yr
ORDER BY yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final concise answer: highest number of motor‑vehicle thefts
--     in any single month for each year 2010–2016
WITH monthly_counts AS (
    SELECT
        EXTRACT(YEAR  FROM date) AS yr,
        EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date) AS mo,
        COUNT(*)                 AS thefts_in_month
    FROM   `bigquery-public-data.chicago_crime.crime`
    WHERE  primary_type = 'MOTOR VEHICLE THEFT'
      AND  EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) BETWEEN 2010 AND 2016
    GROUP  BY yr, mo
)
SELECT yr AS year,
       MAX(thefts_in_month) AS highest_monthly_motor_thefts
FROM   monthly_counts
GROUP  BY year
ORDER  BY year
LIMIT 20;
```
